  "region_note": "One sheet, two materials, and now two parts. The boundary was measured rather than guessed: mean saturation per row of MU's own well.png sits at 0.36 for the top half and 0.55 for the bottom, stepping between them at row 64 of 128 — exactly halfway. Above is the plank roof and the two posts; below is the masonry of the shaft.\n\nBoth halves now wear the same photoscan, the trench-stake wood, at a quarter of a repeat. That is not the split going to waste: what the two parts are for is that the roof is timber and the shaft is rock, and the material is what the derived relief and roughness come from — 0.30 of depth against 0.45, on a roof that is only ever seen from above. One picture, two ways of catching the light.",
